<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uruguay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uruguay is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>. In the early nineteenth century the territory, then known as the Cisplatine Province, was contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, and the costly war over it ended with Uruguayan independence in 1828. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> also note that Uruguay contributed forces alongside Brazil and Argentina in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uruguay.jpg" alt="Uruguay" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Uruguay.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
